<details {{ $attributes->class(['mb-3']) }}>
  <summary class="py-2" style="min-height:44px;cursor:pointer"><x-ctr-mark class="me-2" />How your rating works</summary>
  <div class="mt-2" style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">
    <p>Your Cape Tennis rating estimates your playing strength on a <strong>0–100 scale: higher means stronger</strong>. It is separate from your tournament position or ranking.</p>
    <ul class="ps-3">
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>Who you play matters.</strong> Results are assessed against your opponents’ strength, rather than awarding fixed points for each win.</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>Scores matter too.</strong> A convincing win generally provides stronger evidence than a narrow win, with limits on how much the score margin can influence the calculation.</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>Recent results count more.</strong> We use eligible results from the past two years. A result’s weight halves approximately every six months (180 days).</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>One event has limited influence.</strong> Playing many matches at one tournament cannot overwhelm results from other events.</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>Ratings span age groups within the same ball level.</strong> Red, Orange and CTR (Green/Yellow) always remain separate. Entering a new age group does not reset a rating within that pool. Age and gender do not add or subtract rating points.</li>
      <li class="mb-2"><strong>Only eligible singles evidence in that ball pool counts.</strong> Doubles, byes, walkovers and results with unresolved player identities or invalid scores are excluded. Valid published final placings can provide weaker evidence; they never create played matches. A missing rating never borrows a score from another ball level.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Your <strong>confidence indicator</strong> describes the supporting evidence, not an accuracy percentage. Sparse, older or poorly connected results mean lower confidence. Shared ratings are comparable only between players connected to the same reference group; players with verified results in a disconnected group receive a provisional within-group estimate with low confidence. Matching numbers in different groups do not establish equal ability.</p>
    <p>Ratings can change when new results are added, opponents play, older results lose weight, or scores are corrected—even when you have not recently played.</p>
    <p class="mb-0"><strong>A rating is a provisional estimate, not a guaranteed match prediction or an official selection decision.</strong> It is local to Cape Tennis and is not a conversion to UTR or World Tennis Number.</p>
  </div>
</details>
